<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila posts higher 96 desiccated coconut exports.</title>
<headline>Manila posts higher 96 desiccated coconut exports.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippines posted $78.275 million in export sales of desiccated coconuts last year, up from $68.097 million the previous year, the Philippine Coconut Authority said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It exported 64,785 tonnes of desiccated coconut as against 72,900 tonnes in 1995.</p>
<p>The agency said it expected exports to grow further this year due to the increase in coconut production.</p>
<p>Dessicated coconut is a pure white pared, dehydrated and shredded coconut meat which is being used in confectionery, pastry and bakery products.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 8418938 Fax 8176267</p>
